# Composer implementation handoff

When the user asks for Composer / Composer 2.5 instructions or a TODO list:

- Rank remaining roadmap work. Ship **one** executable slice.
- The TODO list **is** a single copyable XML packet, not a markdown checklist.
- Include bootstrap order, hard out-of-scope rules, implement items, docs, validate commands, and stop.
- Require Composer to **review its diff after execution and fix issues** before handoff.
- Do not commit unless the user asked.

Minimum XML contract:

```xml
<composer_packet model="composer-2.5">
  <ranking>...</ranking>
  <composer_task>
    <follow>...</follow>
    <hard_rules>Do not mark a gate complete unless roadmap exit criteria say so. Do not commit unless asked.</hard_rules>
    <bootstrap order="required">...</bootstrap>
    <goal>...</goal>
    <implement>...</implement>
    <docs>...</docs>
    <validate>...</validate>
    <review required="true">Re-read the plan and diff. Fix defects, missed asserts, stale docs, and MISTAKES.md gaps. Do not start the next slice.</review>
    <stop>...</stop>
  </composer_task>
</composer_packet>
```

When executing such a packet: implement only that slice, then do the review pass and fix findings.
Full template: `AGENTS.md` section "Composer implementation handoff".
